Backend - java
frontend - javaSript

**Cake**
Holds the custom details of each order (flavor, cover, toppings, shape, size and floors). Each attribute has its own price method, and `calculateTotalPrice()` adds them up to get the final price.

**Customer**
Stores the info of the person placing the order, like name and phone number. It's mostly a data class, so it only needs a constructor and getters (and setters if the info can be updated).

**Order**
Links a customer with a cake and stores the order date. It doesn't keep its own price: when needed, it asks the cake for the total, so the price is always calculated in one place.

**Pochita**
The management class. It has no business logic, it only centralizes the calls to the other classes (creating customers, cakes and orders). For now it works as a temporary entry point, and later it's where the endpoints will connect to the frontend.

## Project scope

The backend focuses on the four core classes above, with no database for now. The frontend will be built with JavaScript, turning the project into a web page for managing a bakery.